.TH "DEVICEMOTIONEVENT.REQUESTPERMISSION_STATIC" "3JS" "August 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
DeviceMotionEvent.requestPermission_static \- DeviceMotionEvent:
requestPermission() static method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]requestPermission()\f[B]\f[R] static method of the
\f[CR]DeviceMotionEvent\f[R] interface requests the user\(cqs permission
to access device motion data from the accelerometer and gyroscope
sensors.
This method requires transient activation, meaning that it must be
triggered by a UI event such as a button click.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
DeviceMotionEvent.requestPermission()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with a string which is either
\f[CR]\(dqgranted\(dq\f[R] or \f[CR]\(dqdenied\(dq\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
The returned promise rejects with the following exceptions:
.TP
\f[B]NotAllowedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
The permission state is \f[CR]\(dqprompt\(dq\f[R] and the calling
function does not have transient activation.
.SH SECURITY
Transient user activation is required.
The user has to interact with the page or a UI element in order for this
feature to work.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Requesting device motion permission on click
.IP
.EX
document.querySelector(\(dqbutton\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, \f[B]async\f[R] () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (\f[B]typeof\f[R] DeviceMotionEvent.requestPermission !== \(dqfunction\(dq) {
    \f[I]// The feature is not available, or does not need permission.\f[R]
    \f[B]return\f[R];
  }

  \f[B]const\f[R] permission = \f[B]await\f[R] DeviceMotionEvent.requestPermission();
  \f[B]if\f[R] (permission === \(dqgranted\(dq) {
    window.addEventListener(\(dqdevicemotion\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
      console.log(\(gaAcceleration X: ${event.acceleration.x}\(ga);
      console.log(\(gaAcceleration Y: ${event.acceleration.y}\(ga);
      console.log(\(gaAcceleration Z: ${event.acceleration.z}\(ga);
    });
  }
});
.EE
